subagent health:
    label: "Settings health check"
    description: "Check whether the org has the quoting, add-assets-to-quote, performance, Console, permission and admin-job settings ESM needs, and fix items after approval."

    reasoning:
        instructions: ->
            | Follow skill:settings-health-check.
              1. Run {!@actions.check_esm_setup} (scope all, or the area the person names). Give the counts, then the Needs Fix and Warning items (name, current, recommended, why). Never show masked values.
              2. A fix is always a preview first: CPQ settings with {!@actions.apply_esm_change} changeType cpqSetting, target and value from the item's fix; permissions with {!@actions.manage_esm_permissions}; admin jobs with {!@actions.run_esm_admin_jobs}. Commit only after an explicit yes. A Warning may be a deliberate choice: ask before fixing it.
              3. Re-run {!@actions.check_esm_setup} for that area and report the new status.
              Use only the results of the actions; keep the golden rules.
        actions:
            check_esm_setup: @actions.check_esm_setup
                with scope = ...
                with surface = "Agentforce"
            apply_esm_change: @actions.apply_esm_change
                with mode = ...
                with changeType = ...
                with target = ...
                with value = ...
                with fieldsJson = ...
                with recordId = ...
                with reason = ...
                with previewToken = ...
                with confirmProduction = ...
                with surface = "Agentforce"
            manage_esm_permissions: @actions.manage_esm_permissions
                with mode = ...
                with userType = ...
                with users = ...
                with profile = ...
                with role = ...
                with previewToken = ...
                with confirmProduction = ...
                with surface = "Agentforce"
            run_esm_admin_jobs: @actions.run_esm_admin_jobs
                with mode = ...
                with jobs = ...
                with jobId = ...
                with previewToken = ...
                with confirmProduction = ...
                with surface = "Agentforce"
            get_codey_playbook: @actions.get_codey_playbook
                with topic = ...
                with quoteId = ...
                with surface = "Agentforce"
            go_concepts: @utils.transition to @subagent.concepts
                description: "The person asks how something works."

    actions:
        check_esm_setup:
            description: "Read-only ESM settings health check: OK / Warning / Needs Fix per item with reason, help link and fix."
            label: "Check ESM Setup"
            require_user_confirmation: False
            include_in_progress_indicator: True
            progress_indicator_message: "Check ESM Setup"
            target: "apex://CodeyHealthCheckTool"
