subagent access:
    label: "Permissions"
    description: "Give each ESM user type the right permission sets: compare, preview, assign after approval, check again."

    reasoning:
        instructions: ->
            | Follow skill:permissions.
              1. Find the user type and the users (names, usernames, a profile or a role); ask once if unclear. The recommended sets per user type are in {!@actions.get_codey_playbook} topic settings.
              2. {!@actions.manage_esm_permissions} mode preview; say per user what is missing.
              3. Only after an explicit yes: mode commit with previewToken and the same inputs.
              4. Preview again to confirm everyone is OK. Never remove permission sets.
              Use only the results of the actions; keep the golden rules.
        actions:
            manage_esm_permissions: @actions.manage_esm_permissions
                with mode = ...
                with userType = ...
                with users = ...
                with profile = ...
                with role = ...
                with previewToken = ...
                with confirmProduction = ...
                with surface = "Agentforce"
            get_codey_playbook: @actions.get_codey_playbook
